    {
      "id": "claim_235f037a937f4c04903a6991e528fc8c",
      "statement": "publish_review handles edge cases explicitly: on a 422 unresolved-anchor rejection it drops identifiable offending findings, retries once, and returns unresolvable_findings; an empty re-review with an existing Open SWE summary skips a new summary (skipped_empty_re_review, review_id:null) but still resolves fixed threads and advances last_reviewed_sha; eval mode is a dry_run that posts nothing. Only a numeric review_id with neither flag confirms a real review was posted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
